{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 20}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 106, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a pooling op on the final edge into the output with a 3x3 conv removes a major bottleneck (exp 19: +11 to +19)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 5 is absent, edge 4 is a primary path into the output, so adding a conv there contributes much more (exp 11)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "If the competing path into the output carries only pooling, a conv on edge 4 supplies the missing learned capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 absent, node 2 depends solely on edge 2, so deleting it disconnects the edge-5 path (exp 10)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 0 kills node 1; with edge 1 also absent, only the direct edge 3 path survives (exp 8)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the strongest op, a 3x3 conv, with parameter-free pooling loses the most capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Dropping a pooling edge removes harmful smoothing, while dropping a conv edge loses capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Losing a 3x3 conv on the direct input-to-output edge is very costly (exp 5: -17 to -23)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the conv nearest the output with an identity remov